PAI (since renamed LifeOS) — Daniel Miessler
--------------------------------------------

Upstream: https://github.com/danielmiessler/PAI
          (now https://github.com/danielmiessler/LifeOS)
Licence:  MIT

Two parts of keel are derived from PAI:

  plugins/keel/policy/security.json
      The catalogue of dangerous command patterns, and the blocked / confirm /
      alert tiering that classifies them, are derived from PAI's patterns.yaml.
      The patterns were converted from YAML to JSON regex form rather than
      retyped, so some of them remain close to the originals.

  plugins/keel/hooks/security-guard.mjs
      The design of the guard — matching command *shapes* rather than command
      prefixes, and mapping each tier onto a hook outcome — follows the approach
      of PAI's SecurityValidator.

This is an independent implementation and not a fork. The hook is a fresh
Node.js implementation against the Claude Code PreToolUse interface, and the
behaviour that motivated writing it (the heredoc data-versus-code distinction,
fail-closed policy loading, the path rules, and the alert log) is keel's own.
No upstream source file is vendored into this repository.

